<title>JAPAN: NKK plans 60 bln yen capex in 97/98.</title>
<headline>NKK plans 60 bln yen capex in 97/98.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese steelmaker NKK Corp said on Thursday it plans capital spending of some 60 billion yen for the year starting in April.</p>
<p>The figure is down from estimated capital spending of about 62 billion yen this fiscal year, a company official told reporters.  </p>
<p>The NKK official also said that the company hopes that the company's parent current profit for 1997/98 would be at or above the level of this financial year.</p>
